WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.587
Let’s walk through Population Sentiments.

00:00:02.587 --> 00:00:06.562
Read the published sentiment as audience-specific scenario context.

00:00:06.562 --> 00:00:09.250
Identify who received it, what changed in the narrative

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.975
, and whether the team will respond;

00:00:10.975 --> 00:00:13.750
do not treat sentiment as a hidden score or automatic

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.750
outcome.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:18.312
On this slide, review White Cell-published sentiment updates.

00:00:18.312 --> 00:00:22.250
In practice, sentiment is contextual evidence for participants,

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.600
not deterministic adjudication.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.450
When you are ready, use Open Population Sentiments to

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.113
move to the live surface.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.285
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:32.285 --> 00:00:32.460
.
